6.03 0 0 1-1.013 3.344l-5.654 8.481v15m11.667-16.666h-3.334m-8.333 16.666H8.723A3.333 3.333 0 0 1 5.389 30V20a3.333 3.333 0 0 1 3.334-3.333h4.166"></path></svg></div><div class="sc-d01be8b9-7 hQOaha"><strong>257M</strong></div><div class="sc-d01be8b9-8 jkDDqT"><div class="sc-d01be8b9-9 zwGwX">Votes yes</div></div></div><div data-key-stat-element="true" style="z-index:0" target="_self" class="sc-d01be8b9-5 kQhEbV"><div class="sc-d01be8b9-10 imZPvh"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="40" height="40" fill="none"><path stroke="#3EA2FF" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.333 19.167v4.166m0-4.166v-10a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0m-5 10a2.5 2.5 0 0 0-5 0V22.5c0 6.904 5.597 12.5 12.5 12.5 6.904 0 12.5-5.596 12.5-12.5v-8.333a2.5 2.5 0 0 0-5 0m-10-5v9.166m0-9.166V7.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 5 0v1.667m0 0v9.166m0-9.166a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 5 0v5m0 0v4.166"></path></svg></div><div class="sc-d01be8b9-7 hQOaha"><strong>28.6M</strong></div><div class="sc-d01be8b9-8 jkDDqT"><div class="sc-d01be8b9-9 zwGwX">Votes abstain</div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="about" class="sc-95b88e77-12 bofGKE"><section class="sc-26662a19-0 sc-26662a19-1 iXUvQa ggRJyT"><div data-sticky-two-column="true" data-appearance="default" class="sc-3a69686e-0 hswMK"><div class="sc-3a69686e-1 fFjWHP"><div><h2 class="sc-3e699a48-0 hSEkHu">About this idea</h2><div role="none" aria-label="tags" data-tags-element="true" class="sc-10f390e2-0 yApRb"><a href="/search?withTag=DeFi" class="sc-10f390e2-1 fiBztK">DeFi</a></div><p class="sc-95b88e77-18 iodmTy">NB: Monthly reporting was deprecated from January 2024 and replaced fully by the Milestones Program framework. <a href="https://docs.projectcatalyst.io/fund-documentation/fund10-docs/funded-project-reporting-guideline/funded-projects-accountability-overview" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="sc-95b88e77-22 GXmHC">Learn more here</a></p></div></div><div class="sc-3a69686e-2 cBXzTX"><div data-size="default" class="sc-5df30dce-0 LYCaM"><div class="sc-170e960f-0 iwcLVh"><div id=":R2isr6:" aria-expanded="false" class="sc-bc4a8dd6-0 ddZmjb sc-170e960f-1 gEhaRo"><h3>[Proposal setup] Proposal title</h3>

<p><strong>Please provide your proposal title</strong></p><p>Bifrost: Bitcoin-Cardano bridge secured by Cardano SPOs</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Budget Information</h3>

<p><strong>Enter the amount of funding you are requesting in ADA</strong></p><p>739000</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Time</h3>

<p><strong>Please specify how many months you expect your project to last </strong></p><p>6</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Translation Information</h3>

<p><strong>Please indicate if your proposal has been auto-translated</strong></p><p>No</p>

<p><strong>Original Language</strong></p><p>en</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Problem Statement</h3>

<p><strong>What is the problem you want to solve?</strong></p><p>Cardano's most urgent narrative is becoming the Bitcoin DeFi layer. Cardano needs a permissionless, safe and always live bridge from and to Bitcoin that anyone can use and integrate.</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Supporting Documentation</h3>

<p><strong>Supporting links</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://fluidtokens.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://fluidtokens.com/</a></li>,<li><a href="https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge</a></li>,<li><a href="https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge/tree/main/documentation" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge/tree/main/documentation</a></li>,<li><a href="https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge/blob/main/documentation/litepaperV1.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://github.com/FluidTokens/ft-bifrost-bridge/blob/main/documentation/litepaperV1.pdf</a></li>,<li><a href="https://x.com/FluidTokens/status/1946578539970429300" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://x.com/FluidTokens/status/1946578539970429300</a></li></ul>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Project Dependencies</h3>

<p><strong>Does your project have any dependencies on other organizations, technical or otherwise?</strong></p><p>No</p>

<p><strong>Describe any dependencies or write 'No dependencies'</strong></p><p>No dependencies</p>

<h3>[Proposal Summary] Project Open Source</h3>

<p><strong>Will your project's outputs be fully open source?</strong></p><p>Yes</p>

<p><strong>License and Additional Information</strong></p><p>The product is fully open source under the GPLv3 license.</p>

<h3>[Theme Selection] Theme</h3>

<p><strong>Please choose the most relevant theme and tag related to the outcomes of your proposal</strong></p><p>DeFi</p>

<h3>[Campaign Category] Category Questions</h3>

<p><strong>Describe your established collaborations.</strong></p><p>Our product architecture is the result of months of research from:</p>
<p><strong>FluidTokens</strong> - Their well-known senior team brings technical depth in DeFi, token management, account abstraction and development on both Cardano and Bitcoin.</p>
<p><strong>ZkFold</strong> - Their deep expertise allows proving and verifying Zero Knowledge proofs between Bitcoin and Cardano, running the verifiers on Cardano smart contracts.</p>
<p><strong>Lantr</strong> - Their previous research on this topic allowed the latest design of the Watchtowers, an open set of parties that submit the Bitcoin blocks on Cardano</p>

<p><strong>Describe funding commitments.</strong></p><p>All the partners’ work done so far for Bifrost has been paid by the partners' time and resources: we strongly believe that a proper Bitcoin-Cardano bridge is a public good that crucially benefits the whole Cardano ecosystem.</p>
<p>This grant will accelerate the development of the solution to a point where all the core components will have been developed and released. While we are committed to accomplish this product anyway, this grant allows us to deliver the results much faster, within the proposed timeline.</p>

<p><strong>Describe your key performance metrics.</strong></p><p>Our key metrics for measuring project success include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Number of feedbacks by the Cardano dev community and dApps</li>
<li>Number of feedbacks by the general Cardano community</li>
<li>Number of feedbacks by the Bitcoin community</li>
<li>Amount of volume on the Bifrost bridge from and to Bitcoin</li>
<li>Amount of fees generated</li>
</ul>

<h3>[Your Project and Solution] Solution</h3>

<p><strong>Please describe your proposed solution and how it addresses the problem</strong></p><p>We solve the bridging BTC problem - enabling BTC DeFi on Cardano - with Bifrost, an optimistic bridge that doesn’t suffer of the typical BitVM limitations (1-of-n trust assumption, liveness for pegging-out and granular peg-outs), leveraging Cardano key properties such as eUTxO architecture, Proof-of-Stake and network strong decentralisation level.</p>
<p>The core idea is to leverage Stake Pools (SPOs) consensus to protect the locked BTC on Bitcoin and to move the whole communication, peg-in and peg-out logic on the Cardano side.</p>
<p>SPOs know the Bitcoin confirmed state thanks to the Watchtowers, an open set of players that compete to write the correct chain of new Bitcoin blocks on Cardano. Anyone any time can become a Watchtower, even the user himself.</p>
<p>It’s important to note that Watchtowers cannot forge or change Bitcoin transactions, fully avoiding the risk of scamming SPOs.</p>
<p>In this way, users and institutions can independently peg-in and peg-out without intermediaries, knowing that the pegged-in BTCs are secured by the same entities (the SPOs) that are also already trusted for Cardano security.</p>
<p>The bridge is designed to leverage Cardano, but it can also flawlessly connect Bitcoin to Cardano layer 2s such as Midgard and Sundial.</p>

<h3>[Your Project and Solution] Impact</h3>

<p><strong>Please define the positive impact your project will have on the wider Cardano community</strong></p><p>Bifrost Bitcoin-Cardano bridge will deliver a critical positive impact in all aspects of our beloved community:</p>
<ul>
<li>Cardano dApps: the whole DeFi ecosystem will hugely benefit from the secure and consistent volume of BTCs that will arrive on Cardano looking for yield and other DeFi benefits.</li>
<li>Cardano SPOs: the SPO business model secures the Cardano network and strongly depends on the volume and value of ADA. The strong inflow of BTC will increase both of them dramatically.</li>
<li>Bitcoin users and institutions: BTC holders are desperate to find yield opportunities that don’t sacrifice the permissionless approach. Cardano and Bifrost solve that.</li>
<li>Cardano users: ADA holders will benefit in the appreciation of the Cardano chain and ADA, while also enabling many more opportunities thanks to the increased token volume.</li>
</ul>

<h3>[Your Project and Solution] Capabilities & Feasibility</h3>

<p><strong>What is your capability to deliver your project with high levels of trust and accountability? How do you intend to validate if your approach is feasible?</strong></p><p>All people involved in our teams are highly senior UTxO researchers and developers: our expertise fully covers Cardano and Bitcoin architecture and development, with a proven track record of successful protocols and infrastructure on both chains. We also have dedicated senior expertise in the Zero Knowledge field to ensure that Cardano on-chain validation allows us to prove anything that happens on the Bitcoin side.</p>
<p>All team members are well known and highly regarded in the Cardano community.</p>
<p>FluidTokens is also well known in the Bitcoin community.</p>
<p>We are fully equipped to execute this project from beginning to the end.</p>

<h3>[Milestones] Project Milestones</h3>

<p><strong>Milestone Title</strong></p><p>Bridge Architecture Design Formalization</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Outputs</strong></p><p>Define the bridge core components, the flow of the happy and unhappy paths, the main smart contracts, the main algorithms used for signature aggregation and SPOs communication. Select a few relevant Cardano SPOs to receive ongoing feedback during Bifrost development.</p>

<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul>
<li>Bridge core componenets are properly defined</li>
<li>Happy paths and main unhappy paths are formalized</li>
<li>The smart contracts to develop are defined</li>
<li>The main algorithms have been chosen</li>
<li>Found few relevant SPOs to collaborate</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Evidence of Completion</strong></p><p>The official documentation will be updated to include all these outputs. Collaborating SPOs will be announced.</p>

<p><strong>Delivery Month</strong></p><p>1</p>

<p><strong>Cost</strong></p><p>82000</p>

<p><strong>Progress</strong></p><p>10 %</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Title</strong></p><p>Minimal Testable Version</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Outputs</strong></p><p>This iteration includes the implementation of the happy paths of the Watchtowers that post the Bitcoin confirmed blocks on Cardano, the SPOs on-chain registration, the permissionless peg-ins and the peg-outs.</p>

<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul>
<li>The happy path of Watchtowers behaviour is complete, allowing anyone to be a watchtower and post Bitcoin blocks on Cardano</li>
<li>SPOs registration smart contracts are deployed</li>
<li>Peg-in smart contracts are deployed</li>
<li>Peg-out smart contracts are deployed</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Evidence of Completion</strong></p><p>All smart contracts that involve the Watchtowers happy path, the SPO registration process, the peg-in and the peg-out will be added to the official repository. The Zero Knowledge code of these smart contracts is not included in this milestone.</p>

<p><strong>Delivery Month</strong></p><p>3</p>

<p><strong>Cost</strong></p><p>207000</p>

<p><strong>Progress</strong></p><p>30 %</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Title</strong></p><p>Minimal Usable Version</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Outputs</strong></p><p>This version includes SPOs coordination protocols to aggregate their Bitcoin signatures; the Watchtowers can challenge each other to post the correct Bitcoin fork; Zero Knowledge logic is added to truthfully prove the Bitcoin transactions.</p>

<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul>
<li>SPO coordination protocol is implemented in the dedicated SPO program and allows to aggregate Bitcoin signatures</li>
<li>Watchtower can now challenge each other to post the better Bitcoin fork</li>
<li>Existing smart contracts now implement Zero Knowledge proofs where needed</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Evidence of Completion</strong></p><p>SPO program is now updated in the repository to allow coordination and signatures. </p>
<p>Watchtower program and smart contracts are now updated in the repository to allow fork challenge.</p>
<p>Previous smart contracts now implement the Zero Knowledge code.</p>

<p><strong>Delivery Month</strong></p><p>4</p>

<p><strong>Cost</strong></p><p>164000</p>

<p><strong>Progress</strong></p><p>50 %</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Title</strong></p><p>Minimal Loveable Version</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Outputs</strong></p><p>The unhappy paths and the edge cases are included in this Bifrost iteration, where malicious players, coordination problems and Cardano possible network saturation are correctly managed. Hardening, optimisations and tuning are part of this version.</p>

<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul>
<li>The onchain smart contracts are updated to include unhappy paths and edge cases</li>
<li>The SPO program includes behaviours to manage unhappy paths and restore the normal flow</li>
<li>The Watchtower program takes into account any possible unhappy situation without stopping</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Evidence of Completion</strong></p><p>In the official repository, onchain smart contracts, SPO and Watchtower programs are now updated to include and manage edge cases and unhappy paths, while also being optimised and tuned where needed.</p>

<p><strong>Delivery Month</strong></p><p>5</p>

<p><strong>Cost</strong></p><p>181000</p>

<p><strong>Progress</strong></p><p>80 %</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Title</strong></p><p>Documentation, reporting and full end-to-end execution</p>

<p><strong>Milestone Outputs</strong></p><p>Publish open-source code and architecture documentation, with the evaluation of the bridge security, the edge cases and their mitigations. Execution of the main peg-in and peg-out flows. Create a final poll for SPOs to gather feedback about Bifrost, to check the commitment level and to understand how to proceed for the future incentivization phase.</p>

<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul>
<li>The Bifrost code is fully open source</li>
<li>The documentation describes the whole architecture, the main design choices, a security evaluaion and explanation of the edge cases with their mitigations</li>
<li>A peg-in and a peg-out are executed</li>
<li>SPOs participate in the poll for feedback collection</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Evidence of Completion</strong></p><ul>
<li>All code open sourced in the official repository</li>
<li>All documents present in the official repository</li>
<li>Results of the SPOs poll in a dedicated document</li>
<li>Cardano testnet transactions proving the successful peg-in and peg-out of Bitcoin BTC</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Delivery Month</strong></p><p>6</p>

<p><strong>Cost</strong></p><p>105000</p>

<p><strong>Progress</strong></p><p>100 %</p>

<h3>[Final Pitch] Budget & Costs</h3>

<p><strong>Please provide a cost breakdown of the proposed work and resources</strong></p><ul>
<li><strong>Design and implementation choices - 82,000 ADA</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>This is the most delicate task as a good bridge design must take into account several factors such as the blockchains architecture nuances, the possible saturation levels of Cardano network, the presence of bad participants and the scalability factors.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>On-chain components - 311,000 ADA</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Smart contracts for all the main actions need to be sound, permissionless and avoid concurrency issues, leveraging Cardano strength points and allowing validation, minting of BTC, etc.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Off-chain core components - 241,000 ADA</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Watchtowers monitor the Bitcoin network and post the latest confirmed blocks on Cardano, having to also interact and monitor the Cardano network. The code must be easy to use so anyone can become a Watchtower.</p>
<p>SPOs need to manage their Bitcoin keys, monitor the stake distributions, interact with Cardano smart contracts and coordinate safely.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Documentation and full flow execution - 105,000 ADA</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>This version of the Bifrost bridge must be properly described and open-sourced.</p>
<p>Catalyst reports and milestones management are included here.</p>
<p>Execution of the main end-to-end flows also require some budget</p>

<h3>[Final Pitch] Value for Money</h3>

<p><strong>How does the cost of the project represent value for the Cardano ecosystem?</strong></p><p>The cost of our product Bifrost represents a critical value for Cardano. </p>
<p>Cardano as the Bitcoin DeFi layer is one of the most important and urgent narratives for the ecosystem. A solid safe bridge is the only component that is stopping Cardano to start onboarding real BTC.</p>
<p>On-chain volume, ADA value and new users onboarding will immensely benefit from a secure 2-way bridge that taps into the 2.3 trillion $ Bitcoin ecosystem.</p>
<p>Cardano will also position itself as the first and only top 10 blockchain that is able to directly communicate with Bitcoin.</p>

<h3>[Required Acknowledgements] Consent & Confirmation</h3>

<p><strong>Terms and Conditions:</strong></p><p>Yes</p></div><div data-expanded="false" class="sc-170e960f-3 SPVUA"><button class="sc-170e960f-2 fiRQbZ">+ Read more</button></div></div></div></div></div></section></section><section id="team" class="sc-26662a19-0 sc-26662a19-1 iXUvQa ggRJyT"><h2 class="sc-3e699a48-0 hSEkHu">Team</h2><div class="sc-bc4a8dd6-0 ddZmjb"><ul>
<li>Matteo Coppola: FluidTokens CEO, author of the original first draft of the Bitcoin bridge. Senior smart contract developer and cloud architect.</li>
<li>Raul Rosa Padilla: FluidTokens CTO, co-founder and senior full-stack Cardano developer.</li>
<li>Vladimir Sinyakov: senior Zero Knowledge researcher and developer, as ZkFold team member he is the author of most ZK solutions in the Cardano ecosystem.</li>
<li>Alex Nemish: CTO of Lantr and author of previous attempts to bridge Bitcoin and Cardano</li>
